# Build-context excludes for the ROOT-context images - the dev app /
# dashboard / storefront images in docker-compose.yml build with
# `context: .`, so without these the whole repo ships to the daemon on
# every rebuild. The dashboard's prod image builds from its own context and
# uses apps/dashboard/.dockerignore; a storefront's prod image builds from the
# root too, with the whitelist in its own Dockerfile.prod.dockerignore.
.git/
.claude/
env/*.env
*.md
# DB dumps and one-off reports parked in the repo root.
*.dump
*.html
# air's dev build scratch (~90MB of compiled binaries) + stray `go build`
# output in the module root.
apps/backend/core/tmp/
apps/backend/core/server
.skelet/
# Host trees are hundreds of MB of pure context upload and the images install their
# own musl ones anyway - ** because apps/*/ stops a level short of the storefronts
**/node_modules/
apps/channels/*/.next/
templates/*/.next/
apps/dashboard/dist/
apps/dashboard/.vite/
